1
00:00:14,340 --> 00:00:19,700
A city state was a self -sufficient area ruled by a king or a tyrant -

2
00:00:19,820 --> 00:00:23,860
- the latter only a term for a ruler who conquered power

3
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:27,960
(often with some popular support) instead of inherited it.

4
00:00:28,620 --> 00:00:35,820
The Greece of the time was also considerably larger than today and included parts of the present Turkey

5
00:00:35,920 --> 00:00:39,180
and colonies along large parts of the Mediterranean.

6
00:00:40,120 --> 00:00:46,260
At this time, a number of thinkers appeared who began to question the prevailing truths.

7
00:00:46,620 --> 00:00:50,420
They no longer content themselves with trusting myths and gods tales

8
00:00:50,700 --> 00:00:54,420
Without the help of reason to understand the world.

9
00:00:55,180 --> 00:01:01,400
In the past, knowledge of the myths had been what made the people meaning and guidance in life.

10
00:01:02,020 --> 00:01:10,160
Drought and illness, war and accident, birth and death - everything was due to the belief in the power and influence of the gods.

11
00:01:10,820 --> 00:01:15,160
These myths would be managed and were not allowed to be questioned or changed.

12
00:03:34,360 --> 00:03:38,020
The historians who recorded the fate of the people

13
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:42,420
began to refer to human decisions and natural circumstances

14
00:03:42,780 --> 00:03:47,200
- It was no longer the gods that decided the fate of man, it was herself.

15
00:03:47,960 --> 00:03:52,520
Eventually Greece developed into an economic and military superpower

16
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:55,640
with Athens as the dominant city state.

17
00:03:56,320 --> 00:04:01,840
Here, culture and free debate flourished in a way that was unparalleled in the ancient world.

18
00:04:02,500 --> 00:04:07,460
To this cultural center, thinkers sought from all of the Greek civilization

19
00:04:07,640 --> 00:04:10,380
And now the city ended up in the philosophical eye -catching.

20
00:04:11,180 --> 00:04:17,320
Old traditions and performances were questioned and abandoned - but what would come in its place?

21
00:04:18,160 --> 00:04:22,320
How would one shape the new society and how would man know

22
00:04:22,400 --> 00:04:26,380
Which way she was going to wander now when the gods no longer ruled?
